15cd|n|A blow with the foot or feet; a striking or thrust with the foot. ; The projection on the tang of the blade of a pocket knife, which prevents the edge of the blade from striking the spring. See Illust. of Pocketknife. ; A projection in a mold, to form a depression in the surface of the brick. ; The recoil of a musket or other firearm, when discharged.	n:rnc,63,6~rnc,63,6	N:1ezb,36,2~1ezb,36,2
15cd|v|To strike, thrust, or hit violently with the foot; as, a horse kicks a groom; a man kicks a dog. ; To thrust out the foot or feet with violence; to strike out with the foot or feet, as in defense or in bad temper; esp., to strike backward, as a horse does, or to have a habit of doing so. Hence, figuratively: To show ugly resistance, opposition, or hostility; to spurn. ; To recoil; -- said of a musket, cannon, etc.	o:1irv,17,1~1irv,17,1	d:151o,28,4~151o,28,4
