15dn|v|To deprive of life, animal or vegetable, in any manner or by any means; to render inanimate; to put to death; to slay. ; To destroy; to ruin; as, to kill one's chances; to kill the sale of a book. ; To cause to cease; to quell; to calm; to still; as, in seamen's language, a shower of rain kills the wind. ; To destroy the effect of; to counteract; to neutralize; as, alkali kills acid.	o:1xt9,17,1~1xt9,17,1
